          "by": "sonnet",
          "agrees": false,
          "solution_html": "<p>Triangle OAB isosceles (OA=OB), angle O=40°⇒base angles=70°. Since AB∥CD, transversals OAC and OBD give x=70° (I true) and by symmetry y=70°, so x=y (II true). z at B is vertically opposite the 70° interior angle ABO, so z=70°, hence y+z=140°≠180° (III false).</p>"
        }
